# Leader, Super-Genius: "If a creature you control would connive, instead you draw a card, then that creature connives." (CR 701.50a,
# 614.1a, 614.6) and "At the beginning of combat on your turn, target creature you control connives." Turn 1 Bot1 casts Leader with
# Black Lotus ({U}{U}{U}) and an Island, and at the beginning of its combat Leader connives: Bot1 draws Grizzly Bears (the card the
# replacement draws), then connive draws a Mountain and Bot1 discards. The card the replacement drew can be the one discarded,
# so it was drawn before the discard - Grizzly Bears is a nonland card, and Leader gets a +1/+1 counter (2/4). The connive drew
# once and discarded once, as it was to: the net is two cards in and one out.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Leader, Super-Genius
Island
Savannah Lions
Runeclaw Bear
Hill Giant
Forest
Grizzly Bears
Mountain
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

